    {
      "title": "Hooks Mental Model and Rules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Hooks Mental Model and Rules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a hook is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==hook== is a function whose name starts with `use`",
                "Lets a function component keep {blue:state} and {purple:effects} across renders",
                "React matches hooks to state by ==call order==, not by name"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The two rules",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Rules of hooks",
              "items": [
                "Rule 1: ==top level== only",
                "Never in `if`, loops, nested functions, or after an early `return`",
                "Rule 2: call from components or custom hooks",
                "Never from plain functions or classes"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const [n, setN] = useState(0);",
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  if (on) save(n);",
                "}, [on, n]);"
              ],
              "note": "put the condition inside the hook, never around it"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Each render is a snapshot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Render",
                    "sub": "props, state fixed",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Event",
                    "sub": "handler runs",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "setState",
                    "sub": "schedules render",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New render",
                    "sub": "new values",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inside one render, `count` never changes",
                "A state update does not change it; it ==schedules a new render=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Same hooks, ==same order==, every render. That order is how React finds your state."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "useState and useEffect",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "useState and useEffect",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. useState",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useState(0)`: initial value used ==first render only==",
                "`useState(() => expensive())`: {blue:lazy initializer}",
                "Updates are ==batched==; value changes on the next render",
                "Depends on previous value? Use a ==functional update==",
                "State is **replaced**, not merged: copy with spread, never mutate"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "setCount(c => c + 1);",
                "setUser({ ...user, name });"
              ],
              "note": "new reference, so React sees the change"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. useEffect",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Deps",
                "Runs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "none",
                  "every render"
                ],
                [
                  "`[]`",
                  "once on mount"
                ],
                [
                  "`[a, b]`",
                  "when a or b changes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Runs ==after paint==",
                "Return a ==cleanup==: unsubscribe, clear timers, abort fetches",
                "Cleanup runs before the next effect and on unmount"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  const id = setInterval(tick, 1000);",
                "  return () => clearInterval(id);",
                "}, []);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why `c => c + 1`?** It reads the latest state, not a stale snapshot.",
                "**When does cleanup run?** Before the next effect and on unmount."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "useRef, useMemo and useCallback",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "useRef, useMemo and useCallback",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. useRef: a box that never re-renders",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useRef(init)` returns a ==stable== `{ current }` object",
                "Changing `ref.current` does {red:not} trigger a re-render",
                "Use it for ==DOM nodes== and mutable values: timer IDs, the previous value"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const inputRef = useRef(null);",
                "<input ref={inputRef} />",
                "<button onClick={() => inputRef.current.focus()}>",
                "  Focus",
                "</button>"
              ],
              "note": "ref={inputRef} fills current with the DOM node"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. useMemo vs useCallback",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Hook",
                "Caches",
                "Recomputes when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`useMemo(() => compute(a, b), [a, b])`",
                  "a **value**",
                  "a or b changes"
                ],
                [
                  "`useCallback(fn, deps)`",
                  "a **function identity**",
                  "deps change"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useCallback(fn, deps)` equals ==`useMemo(() => fn, deps)`==",
                "Useful with `React.memo` children",
                "Useful as an effect dependency"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. When to memoize",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Hint, not a guarantee",
              "text": "Memoization is a ==performance hint==. Add it only after **measuring** a real cost or an identity problem."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "useReducer, useContext and Custom Hooks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "useReducer, useContext and Custom Hooks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. useReducer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const [state, dispatch] = useReducer(reducer, init)`",
                "Prefer it over useState for ==related fields== or ==many transitions==",
                "`dispatch({ type: 'add', payload })` is the ==only way== to change state",
                "Reducer is {red:pure}: return a **new object**, never mutate"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "function reducer(state, action) {",
                "  switch (action.type) {",
                "    case 'add':",
                "      return { ...state, items: [...state.items, action.payload] };",
                "    default:",
                "      return state;",
                "  }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. useContext",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useContext(Ctx)` reads the nearest `<Ctx.Provider value>`",
                "Value changes → ==every consumer re-renders==",
                "So **memoize** the value object"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const value = useMemo(() => ({ user, setUser }), [user]);",
                "return <Ctx.Provider value={value}>{children}</Ctx.Provider>;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Custom Hooks",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Function named ==useX== that calls other hooks: `useFetch`, `useLocalStorage`",
                "Each call gets its own **independent** state"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Custom hook",
                "Context"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Shares",
                  "logic",
                  "state"
                ],
                [
                  "Two components",
                  "{red:separate} values",
                  "{green:same} value"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Logic, not state",
              "text": "Two components calling `useFetch` do **not** share values. To share them, put the state in ==context=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Hook Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Hook Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Stale and Looping Effects",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Stale closure==: missing deps read **old** state; list the deps or use a functional update",
                "==Infinite loop==: `setState` in an effect with no deps, or an object/array literal in deps",
                "Updater form `setN(n => n + 1)` needs no `n` in deps"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  const id = setInterval(() => setN(n => n + 1), 1000);",
                "  return () => clearInterval(id);",
                "}, []);"
              ],
              "note": "no stale n, no dep needed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Identity and Mutation",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Effect",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Literal `{}`, `[]` or `() => {}` in deps",
                  "new each render; breaks `useMemo`, `useCallback`, `React.memo`",
                  "memoize it"
                ],
                [
                  "`arr.push(x)` or `obj.x = 1`, then `setState(same)`",
                  "same reference, {red:no re-render}",
                  "copy: `[...arr, x]`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Fetch Races",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No cleanup: a ==late response== overwrites newer state",
                "Use an ignore flag or ==AbortController=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  let ignore = false;",
                "  fetch(url).then(r => r.json())",
                "    .then(d => { if (!ignore) setData(d); });",
                "  return () => { ignore = true; };",
                "}, [url]);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Fresh **deps**, fresh **copies**, **cleanup** every effect."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "React Hooks Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "React Hooks Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. State and effects",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`useState(init)`",
                  "`[v, setV]`; use `setV(prev => next)` when it depends on the previous value"
                ],
                [
                  "`useEffect(fn)`",
                  "runs {red:every render}"
                ],
                [
                  "`useEffect(fn, [])`",
                  "runs on {green:mount only}"
                ],
                [
                  "`useEffect(fn, [x])`",
                  "runs {blue:when x changes}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Return a cleanup function== from the effect",
                "It runs before the next effect and on unmount"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Refs, caches, reducers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Hook",
                "Remember"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`useRef`",
                  "mutable box, ==no re-render==; DOM nodes, persistent values"
                ],
                [
                  "`useMemo`",
                  "caches a ==value=="
                ],
                [
                  "`useCallback`",
                  "caches a ==function=="
                ],
                [
                  "`useReducer`",
                  "`dispatch(action)` into a ==pure== reducer"
                ],
                [
                  "`useContext`",
                  "reads the ==nearest Provider== value"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Call hooks at the ==top level== only: no if, loops, nested functions",
                "Call them only in ==components== or ==custom hooks==",
                "Custom hooks are named `useX`; each call has its **own state**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "React matches hooks by ==call order==, so keep that order identical on every render."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "With n = 0, one click runs `setN(n + 1); setN(n + 1);`. What is n on the next render?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "**1**, not 2: both calls read the same snapshot, n = 0",
                "`setN(c => c + 1)` twice gives 2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`useEffect(() => { setInterval(() => setC(c + 1), 1000) }, [])` starts with c = 0. What does c show after 5 seconds?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "**1**, and it stays there: the closure captured c = 0 on mount",
                "Fix: `setC(x => x + 1)`, and return a cleanup that clears the interval"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`items.push(x); setItems(items)` shows no change on screen. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Same reference, so React sees no change and skips the re-render",
                "Fix: `setItems([...items, x])`"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}